            <div xml:id="d449">

                <pb facs="0580" n="478" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg478"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 13815/61.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Minister
                    Dodge.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1908-06-26"><hi rendition="#italic">June 26,
                        1908</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Reference your telegram of the 25th instant, you can inform Honduranean
                    Government that President’s warrants have been mailed to American consul, Puerto
                    Cortez, said warrants authorizing Peter W. Beery as agent of this Government to
                    receive Francis G. Bailey, Albert W. Bailey, Alfred Oxley, and Herbert H. Meyers
                    (the name Herbert being fictitious). Greeley, vice consul, has been informed
                    that department has no objection to his taking temporary possession <pb
                        facs="0581" n="479" xml:id="pg479"/> in his individual capacity of <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Goldsboro</hi> and cargo pending arrival at Puerto
                    Cortez of a duly accredited agent of the creditors authorized to take steps
                    necessary to secure and have charge of return of vessel to United States.
                    Department can not permit Beery as presidential agent to return on <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Goldsboro</hi> and has so informed New York
                    representatives of the creditors.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Adee.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
